  "name": "Question 17",
  "problem": "Fill in the correct options below to solve the congruence $40x≡7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,333).$\n\nSince $\\text{gcd}(40,333)=$\n{{field-1}}, \nusing the extended Euclidean algorithm, we get \n\n| $1\\,=\\,40\\,\\cdot ($\n{{field-2}}\n$)+\\,333\\,\\cdot ($\n{{field-3}}\n$).$ |\n| --- |\n\nTherefore, expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $333,$ the solution to the congruence is  \n\n| $x≡$\n{{field-4}}\n$(\\text{mod}\\,333).$ |\n| --- |",
